@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam roundcorner 14
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.8
skinparam titleFontSize 19
skinparam titleFontStyle bold

title Growth on Demand — How Capacity Is Added Without Redesign

rectangle "TODAY — Proven\n(measured & tested)" as T0 #DCFCE7 {
  component "1 write leader\n+ 1 live mirror" as A1
  component "Read capacity spread\nacross every node" as A2
}

rectangle "STEP 1 — Low effort\n(add read nodes)" as T1 #DBEAFE {
  component "Grow reporting and\ncustomer enquiries" as B1
  component "No change to any\napplication" as B2
}

rectangle "STEP 2 — Low risk\n(before volume forces it)" as T2 #FEF3C7 {
  component "Divide the business into\nindependent parts by customer" as C1a
  component "Each part keeps its own\nleader + own mirror" as C2a
}

rectangle "STEP 3 — Required for\nregulated deployment" as T3 #FFE4E6 {
  component "Zero-lag confirmation\nbefore a change is final" as D1a
  component "Remove the single\ngateway as a bottleneck" as D2a
}

rectangle "STEP 4 — Independent\nrecovery procedures" as T4 #FCE7F3 {
  component "Automatic rebuild of a\ndiscarded node" as E1a
}

T0 -[#22C55E]-> T1 : "read volume grows"
T1 -[#0EA5E9]-> T2 : "write volume grows"
T2 -[#F59E0B]-> T3 : "regulatory requirement"
T3 -[#DC2626]-> T4 : "operational maturity"

note bottom of T0 #F0FDF4
  **What scales first, and why:**
  enquiries are cheap to add and carry no risk.
  Recording changes is the expensive axis —
  it is scaled last, by dividing the business
  into parts, never by making one server faster.
end note

note bottom of T2 #FFFBEB
  **Key business property:** growth is bought in
  steps, each of which is reversible and none of
  which requires applications to be rewritten.
end note

@enduml